# `isLoud(kind)` is sixteen `kind === written number` joined by `||`. The walk makes ONE Switch of three and more such equalities of one value, and a written switch weighs half its targets; the scan weighed each equality as an operation: sixteen: over the limit of leaves copied in loops (twelve and the operands), so the helper stayed a call in every turn. In a loop the chain now weighs what its Switch weighs (eight) and the helper is copied: countLoud() holds the Switch and no call. Outside loops nothing changes: once() calls it (no bytes for time outside loops).
